    <div class="tg-hero__inner">
      <span class="tg-hero__type">Part V of Five</span>
      <h1 class="tg-hero__title">Keeping the Fire, and the Way Back</h1>
      <p class="tg-hero__intro">
        Faith rarely ends in a decision. It cools, the way a house cools when nobody
        adds fuel — and the people it happens to are usually the last to notice. This
        part is about the ordinary mechanics of staying warm: what the first love is
        and how it is recovered, the seven churches as a diagnostic, the means God
        actually uses to keep his people, and the road back for anyone who has already
        gone a long way off.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="tg-hero__key-verse">
        <p>Remember therefore from where you have fallen; repent, and do the works you
           did at first.</p>
        <cite><a class="ref" data-ref="Revelation 2:5">Revelation 2:5</a></cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
